1" source="c29" target="c10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c62" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=0;endSize=16;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#000000;exitX=0;exitY=0.35;entryX=1;entryY=0.35;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c55" target="c44"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c63" value="&lt;b&gt;Notation:&lt;/b&gt; UML 2.5 use case diagram. Stick figures are actors (user classes); ellipses inside the box are use cases of Tuklas; a line links an actor to the use cases it starts. A hollow arrow is generalization: a Student can also do what a Visitor does, an Educator what a Student does, and a Super-admin what an Admin does. Every member also signs in and manages their account (Section 4.1)." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#ffffff;fontSize=14;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10" y="980" width="1290" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>